            "review_title": "Review at Pho24 Restaurant",
            "review_text": "fernisi100\nNottingham, United Kingdom62 contributions\n0\nExcellent Quality Pho in a restaurant chain\nFeb 2020 • Couples\nWe popped in for a quick meal as a change from the Ben Thành Street Food Market and weren’t disappointed. This is a restaurant chain franchise but isn’t lacking in quality. Pick the size of your bowl (medium or large), type of pho (brisket, chicken, vegetarian, meat balls), a side (fresh spring rolls, fried spring rolls, shredded pork, vegetable), your pud (flan, yogurt, taro, red bras in yogurt), your drink (loads and loads) as if your off!\n\nWe opted for the vegetarian and beef pho, taro in yogurt and flan, fresh and fried spring rolls and beers and the food was served in minutes followed by extra rice later to mop up the amazing pho stock in the bowls. \n\nInexpensive and fab restaurant was full of locals which is always a good sign and we were stuffed and ready for a nighttime walk along the nearby Nguyen Hue, five it a try as a change from the Ben Thành Street Food Market or just a quick lunch.\nRead more\nWritten February 10, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
